Keep wasm-merge's state per thread, and let an embedder own the module.

`wasm-merge.cpp` merges into a `Module` at file scope, and keeps the start
functions, the export mode and the origin of each export beside it. A command
line tool merges once per process, so there that is safe. An embedder merges
into a module it read itself, and may merge two pairs on two threads at once --
a test harness does.

Make `merged` a pointer per thread, which `main` points at a module of its own
and the bridge at the caller's, and make the other three `thread_local`. A
call sets every one of them before it reads it.

--- a/src/tools/wasm-merge.cpp
